<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="011" project="spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI">
  <metadata>
    <title>Fix the DI-lifetime hazard and record the ADR-009 cache decision (FR-A2)</title>
    <phase>1 Prerequisites</phase>
    <gate>003 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>auth tag, modifies .cs + DI registrations; blocks the credential swap.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified with a named reference implementation to copy.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>CORRECTED 2026-08-20: NOT parallel-safe. Task 010 also modifies src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseAccessDataSource.cs. Dispatching both as concurrent sub-agents would collide on that file. Run 010 then 011 sequentially -- 011's CCA caching builds on the branch structure 010 corrects.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>003</deps>
    <tags>auth,bff-api,dataverse,di,bugfix</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>DataverseAccessDataSource is a transient typed HttpClient (SpaarkeCore.cs:39) and AgentTokenService is scoped (AgentModule.cs:24), so each builds a fresh MSAL confidential client per resolution and discards its token cache. Client assertions require shared, cached clients. Fix both to singleton-cached CCAs and record the ADR-009 interaction decision.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with MSAL token-cache and ASP.NET DI-lifetime experience.</role>
  <goal>Both types reuse a process-wide static CCA keyed (tenant|client), with the ADR-009 caching decision written down rather than inherited by accident.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Client assertions need shared/cached clients — a per-request CCA discards the token cache and re-acquires on every call. DataverseUserClient.cs:55-56,91 already solved exactly this with a process-wide static CCA cache; that is the pattern to copy, not to reinvent. Independently correct regardless of the credential decision.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/Dataverse/DataverseUserClient.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/SpaarkeCore.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AgentModule.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Agent/AgentTokenService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseAccessDataSource.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/GraphTokenCache.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="003" status="pending">Credential decision recorded</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: copy the static CCA cache keyed (tenant|client) from DataverseUserClient.cs:55-56,91. Do not invent a second caching shape.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-009">Scope: MSAL's in-process token cache inside a singleton CCA is PER-INSTANCE, while GraphTokenCache.cs:21 already implements a Redis (IDistributedCache) OBO token cache. This task MUST record which is authoritative — serialize MSAL's cache into IDistributedCache, or leave GraphTokenCache as the sole cross-request cache. Silence is not an acceptable outcome. Dev is single-instance so it does not bite in scope, but the decision must be explicit.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: changing a lifetime is not a licence to add registrations. Keep the registration count flat.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: do not change the credential TYPE — that is Phase 2. Lifetime only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: coverage to tests/integration/seam/**. DI-registration tests are banned; assert behaviour (same CCA instance across two resolutions) not container wiring.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>MSAL client caching, DI lifetimes, Redis token cache</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-009-caching-redis-first.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/CREDENTIAL-INVENTORY.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read DataverseUserClient.cs:50-100 to capture the static-cache pattern.</step>
    <step>Apply it to DataverseAccessDataSource; change SpaarkeCore.cs:39 registration accordingly.</step>
    <step>Apply it to AgentTokenService; change AgentModule.cs:24 from scoped to singleton.</step>
    <step>Investigate the GraphTokenCache interaction and DECIDE + WRITE DOWN the ADR-009 position.</step>
    <step>Add a seam test proving two resolutions share the underlying CCA.</step>
    <step>Verify publish size + CVE scan.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Making AgentTokenService singleton surfaces captured scoped dependencies (a captive-dependency error at startup) — STOP and report rather than widening other lifetimes to compensate.</trigger>
    <trigger>The ADR-009 decision implies multi-instance token-cache work beyond this project's dev-only scope — record it and escalate rather than building it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseAccessDataSource.cs</output>
    <output type="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Agent/AgentTokenService.cs</output>
    <output type="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/SpaarkeCore.cs</output>
    <output type="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AgentModule.cs</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/decisions/011-adr009-token-cache-decision.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <!-- AMENDED 2026-08-20 during execution, per CLAUDE.md 8.5 closed-set rule: the original pair read
         "resolving X twice FROM DI yields the same underlying CCA instance". Neither half is provable
         as authored -- resolving from a container is ADR-038 ban B3, and comparing the private _cca
         field across instances is ban B8. Amending the criteria to what IS provable, rather than
         marking the originals complete against different evidence. The substitute is stronger: it
         counts BUILDS per key, so it also catches a GetOrAdd factory that ran twice. -->
    <criterion>Constructing DataverseAccessDataSource N times with one (tenant|client|secret) builds EXACTLY ONE confidential client, asserted per-key so concurrent tests cannot perturb it.</criterion>
    <criterion>Constructing AgentTokenService N times with one (tenant|client|secret) builds EXACTLY ONE confidential client.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative: two different tenants get two different clients -- sharing is keyed, so token caches cannot cross a tenant boundary.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative: a ROTATED secret builds a new client rather than silently reusing the stale one (the secret participates in the cache key).</criterion>
    <criterion>The ADR-009 decision is written down with its reason.</criterion>
    <criterion>No behaviour change beyond token-cache reuse; the existing test suite stays green.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: no captive-dependency error at startup; the app boots cleanly.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: OBO still fails CLOSED for an unauthorised user.</criterion>
    <criterion>Publish size reported; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Completed 2026-08-20. FULL rigor. Full suite 10,549/0; ArchTests 36/36; publish 43.68 MB compressed
    incl. PDBs (+0.01, 1.28 MB below the 44.96 baseline, ceiling 60); CVE clean.

    TWO AUTHORED STEPS WERE WRONG FOR THE CODE AND WERE ADAPTED (steps mode=directional):
    (1) SpaarkeCore.cs:39 was NOT changed. It is AddHttpClient&lt;T&gt; -- promoting a typed HttpClient to
    singleton pins one HttpMessageHandler for process lifetime AND, decisively, this type holds mutable
    per-instance auth state (_currentToken, the Authorization header), so a singleton is a data race
    that can bleed a token between users. Sharing is achieved by a static cache instead.
    (2) The app-only credential was assumed safe because Program.cs:46 registers TokenCredential
    singleton. True of the MI branch ONLY -- the secret branch built a ClientSecretCredential per
    request. Caught at code review (W-3); now cached.

    ADR-009 DECIDED: application-level caches stay authoritative; NOT wiring AddDistributedTokenCache
    (a serialized MSAL cache carries refresh-token material -- a security-posture change that must not
    ride along with a DI-lifetime fix). Consequences, two revisit triggers and the preferred remedy per
    trigger are recorded. Escalation trigger 2 fired and was handled as prescribed: recorded, not built.

    ALSO FIXED HERE: a task-010 regression. Its fail-fast validation broke 13 ExternalAccess contract
    tests via a stub relying on the removed silent fallback. Generalised into .claude/FAILURE-MODES.md
    AP-7.

    BOOKED ONWARD: task 060 gets the source-analysis guard that no call site bypasses the cache (2nd
    such obligation, alongside 010's). Tasks 020 AND 022 carry the CCA-consolidation obligation as a
    constraint + acceptance criterion -- task 011 leaves three per-class caches, accepted only as a
    TIME-BOXED ADR-028 A4 path-A exception EXPIRING AT 022.

    Acceptance criteria 1-2 were amended during execution per CLAUDE.md 8.5: as authored they required
    proof by DI resolution (ADR-038 ban B3) or private-field comparison (ban B8), neither provable.

    Record: notes/decisions/011-adr009-token-cache-decision.md
  </notes>
</task>
